.TH DEEPWIN 1 "October 2026" "DeepWin" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
deepwin \- configure Deepin desktop features
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deepwin
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
DeepWin is a native DTK panel for clipboard paste, desktop shortcuts,
window previews, calculator decimal input and optional Claude/Z.AI tools.
Features are enabled by the user; installation does not activate them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show available options.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the program version.
.TP
.B \-\-smoke\-test
Query states, check that the window opens, and exit without changing settings.
Unavailable optional features are accepted.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-integrations
Require all integrations to be available during a smoke test.
.TP
.BI \-\-section " section"
Open overview, productivity, appearance or tools.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.local/state/devedu.deepin-configs/
contains restoration backups. User XDG directory overrides are supported.
The persistent integration runtime is kept under
.I ~/.local/share/devedu.deepin-configs/runtime/.
.SH RESTORATION
Use the restore button before removing the GUI, or run
.I ~/.local/share/devedu.deepin-configs/runtime/current/bin/deepwin-restore
from the user's graphical session after removing it.
